<title>BELGIUM: DECEUNINCK 1996 PROFIT UP 29.6 PCT.</title>
<headline>DECEUNINCK 1996 PROFIT UP 29.6 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			    464  vs    358</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		     59  vs     56</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian polyvinyl chloride (PVC) profiles producer Deceuninck Plastics Industries NV said in a statement the results of Slocomb Industries Inc were entirely consolidated in 1996. In 1995 only five months of results had been included.  </p>
<p>    Turnover				  5,874   vs  5,322</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			    774   vs    581</p>
<p>    Current net cashflow		  1,219   vs    862</p>
<p>    Operating profit			  888   vs    650</p>
<p>    Provisions, write-downs		 115   vs    n/a</p>
<p>    Equity *				  3,494  vs   2,710</p>
<p>NOTE - Deceuninck said that provisions and write-downn will be used for reorganisations and for large-scale maintenance and repair works in western Europe and North America.</p>
<p>* 1995 equity excluded the effect of new depreciation rules.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
